-- Regression fixture entry for MARCH_LIB_PATH reachability pruning.
-- Deliberately does NOT reference the ill-typed lib module (see
-- libpath_ill_typed/): auto-discovery used to parse+typecheck every .march
-- file on the lib path regardless of reachability, so a type error in an
-- UNRELATED module failed this build.  The resolver now prunes auto-discovered
-- modules the entry cannot reach, so --check must exit 0 (the ill-typed module
-- is dropped, not compiled).
--
-- NOTE: reachability is over-approximated from the raw source text, so this
-- comment must NOT spell the ill-typed module's declared name, or the token
-- scan would treat it as referenced and keep it in the build.
mod LibpathEntry do
  needs IO.Console

  fn main(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console)) do
    println("ok: unrelated ill-typed lib module is pruned, not built")
  end

end
